# Feedback

Give people a quiet, clearly named route to report problems with a page or task.

## One delivery and privacy contract

This page owns feedback delivery behaviour; the [publishing feedback variant](../publishing/components/feedback.html) keeps its contextual form and public issue examples.

Before offering a submission, identify its real destination and whether it is public. Ask only for information the receiving service needs. Confirm receipt only from the service’s successful response; an accepted request awaiting a response is still pending. Preserve the comment on failure and do not send it again automatically. If delivery is uncertain, explain that uncertainty before inviting a retry that could duplicate a report.

A local preview acknowledgement must say that nothing was sent. A link to the public repository remains navigation, with its privacy context visible before activation. A household warning uses the [status and notice decision guide](status.html), not this feedback channel.

## When to use

Place feedback after the main task or article. It should be available without interrupting device controls or requiring a positive rating. Distinguish product feedback from urgent household alerts and technical support.

The official GOV.UK component is in trial. Our adaptation uses a short invitation and a direct route to a maintained channel. Do not imply that someone monitors feedback continuously unless that is true.

